Stamp frames in CLOCK_MONOTONIC time.

V4L2 capture buffers are expected to carry CLOCK_MONOTONIC timestamps. With
base time set to "now", buffers written to v4l2loopback carry pipeline running
time (seconds since the relay started), and consumers such as ffmpeg/ffplay
convert those into large negative timestamps. A zero base time makes running
time equal to the monotonic system clock.

--- a/src/v4l2-relayd.c
+++ b/src/v4l2-relayd.c
@@ -426,7 +426,7 @@ output_pipeline_create ()
 
   clock = gst_system_clock_obtain ();
   gst_pipeline_use_clock (GST_PIPELINE (pipeline), clock);
-  gst_element_set_base_time (pipeline, gst_clock_get_time (clock));
+  gst_element_set_base_time (pipeline, 0);
   gst_element_set_start_time (pipeline, GST_CLOCK_TIME_NONE);
   gst_object_unref (clock);
 
